    "S0": {
      "headline": "A modest AI plateau leaves ordinary pay and employer risks in view",
      "whatTheyDo": [
        {
          "tag": "keep-going",
          "text": "Wendy Lopez plans to keep fixing timesheet tickets and may take the PHP course her tutor recommended."
        },
        {
          "tag": "save-more",
          "text": "Erik Reyes plans to try saving a hundred a month with his partner Lina."
        },
        {
          "tag": "cut-spending",
          "text": "Marco Dubois plans to skip the summer holiday and cook at home with his partner Ana."
        },
        {
          "tag": "learn-ai",
          "text": "Emeka Ziegler plans to try setting up the AI chat to write test data by year-end."
        },
        {
          "tag": "side-income",
          "text": "Sara Jensen plans to grow the website side business to five customers a month."
        }
      ],
      "whatTheySay": [
        "**Wendy Lopez**: I'd say **I told you so** about the AI hype in our team group chat.",
        "**Gareth Kowalski**: I see **AI Plateau** as routine help while clients still need people who understand shifts."
      ],
      "whatTheyThink": [
        "**156 of 243** privately weigh wages, bills or savings even in a plateau.",
        "**47 of 243** privately weigh skills, employers or local job security.",
        "**24 of 243** privately expect familiar work or earnings to continue."
