    "S3": {
      "headline": "Five years opens preparation time, while paid alternatives remain conditional",
      "whatTheyDo": [
        {
          "tag": "change-job",
          "text": "Sara Jensen plans to keep her developer wage while building side income and savings, then look at building trade work around 2029."
        },
        {
          "tag": "retrain",
          "text": "Wendy Lopez plans to start the electrical installation night course while keeping her Paybridge wage to pay for it."
        },
        {
          "tag": "save-more",
          "text": "Erik Reyes plans to sell the old gaming PC and second bike to build savings."
        },
        {
          "tag": "keep-going",
          "text": "Marco Dubois plans to learn the invoice code from colleague Kofi before Kofi retires."
        },
        {
          "tag": "side-income",
          "text": "Colin Quinn plans to start freelancing to set up AI tools for small local firms."
        }
      ],
      "whatTheySay": [
        "**Wendy Abbott**: I see **AGI by 2031** as five years to learn appointment support.",
        "**Gareth Tanaka**: I'd ask for **paid shadow time** and technician permission before training."
      ],
      "whatTheyThink": [
        "**86 of 243** privately see coding wages or roles at risk by 2031.",
