    "S4": {
      "headline": "A decade offers room to prepare, but current bills and later work still matter",
      "whatTheyDo": [
        {
          "tag": "save-more",
          "text": "Erik Reyes plans to build two months of savings in the first year."
        },
        {
          "tag": "keep-going",
          "text": "Marco Dubois plans to take over colleague Kofi’s invoice module when Kofi retires in 2029."
        },
        {
          "tag": "change-job",
          "text": "Dana Bauer plans to look at hospital software training jobs while keeping her Ledgerline wage."
        },
        {
          "tag": "retrain",
          "text": "Wendy Lopez plans to start the part-time electrical course around year three while still employed at Paybridge."
        },
        {
          "tag": "collective-action",
          "text": "Emeka Ziegler plans to stay active in the Carely union branch."
        }
      ],
      "whatTheySay": [
        "**Wendy Olsen**: I'd protect **rider appeals** when fare software changes and a junior coder may no longer handle disputes.",
        "**Gareth Dubois**: I want **paid trade openings** checked before AGI reaches code in 2036."
      ],
      "whatTheyThink": [
        "**107 of 243** privately still weigh current wages and household costs.",
        "**73 of 243** privately see time to build skills, savings or another path.",
        "**38 of 243** privately refuse to assume retirement income or children’s wages."
